{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"17","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Hierarchy"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"64 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Nick's company employed "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" people. Now Nick needs to build a tree hierarchy of «supervisor-surbodinate» relations in the company (this is to say that each employee, except one, has exactly one supervisor). There are "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" applications written in the following form: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"«employee "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" is ready to become a supervisor of employee "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bi"},{"kind":"text","text":" at extra cost "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ci"},{"kind":"text","text":"»"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". The qualification "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"qj"},{"kind":"text","text":" of each employee is known, and for each application the following is true: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"qai > qbi"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Would you help Nick calculate the minimum cost of such a hierarchy, or find out that it is impossible to build it."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first input line contains integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n ≤ 1000"},{"kind":"text","text":") — amount of employees in the company. The following line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" space-separated numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"qj"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ qj ≤ 106"},{"kind":"text","text":")— the employees' qualifications. The following line contains number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ m ≤ 10000"},{"kind":"text","text":") — amount of received applications. The following "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contain the applications themselves, each of them in the form of three space-separated numbers: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bi"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ci"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ ai, bi ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ ci ≤ 106"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Different applications can be similar, i.e. they can come from one and the same employee who offered to become a supervisor of the same person but at a different cost. For each application "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"qai > qbi"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output the only line — the minimum cost of building such a hierarchy, or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if it is impossible to build it."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n7 2 3 1\n4\n1 2 5\n2 4 1\n3 4 1\n1 3 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"11\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n1 2 3\n2\n3 1 2\n3 1 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"-1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample one of the possible ways for building a hierarchy is to take applications with indexes 1, 2 and 4, which give 11 as the minimum total cost. In the second sample it is impossible to build the required hierarchy, so the answer is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"17B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/17/problem/B"}